cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this design or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "Drone-Stabilized Passive Dynamic Walker (open-source hardware)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Ishida"
    given-names: "Eiri"
abstract: >
  A McGeer-type kneed passive dynamic walker stabilized attitude-only from
  above the virtual pivot point: by drone thrust (Gen-1) or partial helium
  buoyancy (Gen-2 spherical envelope, Gen-3 airship hull with cruciform
  tail). The passive limit cycle is preserved; buoyancy is kept within the
  37-94% weight operating window (52%W recommended) so the legs remain
  loaded; horizontal fan thrust replaces the slope as the energy top-up.
  Includes FreeCAD sources, engineering drawings, PyBullet physics/control
  code, gait trajectories, and videos.
keywords:
  - passive dynamic walking
  - buoyancy stabilization
  - virtual pivot point
  - open source hardware
